# F. Cost. Same WHIP VP8 route, cap 2.5 Mbit/s, 1280x720@30 fixture. Probe is harness raw, video track bytes only.
# A keyframe byte is the first frame of each MoQ group. Window is the raw subscriber's wall span (~8 s).
# quality_difference=missing (no PSNR/SSIM alignment against the y4m was run).
#
# policy=off:       frames=239 groups=1 share=0.0061 bitrate=1536.7 kbps wall_ms=7986. Gate sends: none.
# policy=trial:     frames=238 groups=4 share=0.0411 bitrate=1578.3 kbps wall_ms=7900. Gate: period x4 (~2 s).
# policy=saturated: frames=236 groups=8 share=0.1098 bitrate=1638.1 kbps wall_ms=7881. Gate: period-bit x8 (~1 s).
#
# Bitrate minus off: trial +41.6 kbps, saturated +101.4 kbps.
# Share minus off: trial +0.0350, saturated +0.1037.
# The saturated row is KEYFRAME_POLICY=saturated, which sets keyframes.saturate and floor=1s.
# The log still says causes=["period"] because the floor wake reuses the period cause bit.
# The cadence separates them: 8 sends in ~8 s against trial's 4. A 1 s period is not this hook;
# on_keyframe would restart that period, and off sent nothing.
